{"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Anyone who has ever met her thought she was absolutely beautiful.","bold_text_offsets":[[55,64]],"type":"example"},{"text":"There's a beautiful lake by the town.","bold_text_offsets":[[10,19]],"type":"example"},{"text":"[A]s amongſt the Moores, the Iettieſt blacke are deem'd / The beautifulſt of them; […]","ref":"1622, Michael Drayton, “The Sixe and Twentieth Song”, in The Second Part, or A Continuance of Poly-Olbion from the Eighteenth Song. […], London: […] Augustine Mathewes for Iohn Marriott, Iohn Grismand, and Thomas Dewe, →OCLC, page 124:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[62,73]]},{"text":"“Is Olga de Coude very beautiful?” she asked. And Tarzan laughed and kissed her again. “Not one-tenth so beautiful as you, dear,” he said.","ref":"1913, Edgar Rice Burroughs, The Return of Tarzan, New York: Ballantine Books, published 1963, page 214:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[23,32],[105,114]]},{"text":"It's rather like a beautiful Inverness cloak one has inherited. Much too good to hide away, so one wears it instead of an overcoat and pretends it's an amusing new fashion.","ref":"1963, Margery Allingham, chapter 5, in The China Governess: A Mystery, London: Chatto & Windus, →OCLC:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[19,28]]},{"text":"It is a beautiful kitchen! — It is beautiful.","ref":"2016, VOA Learning English (public domain):","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[8,17],[35,44]]}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 1520s","references":[]}],"glosses":["Possessing beauty, impressing the eye; attractive."]},{"examples":[{"text":"the house beautiful","bold_text_offsets":[[10,19]],"type":"example"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 1520s","references":[]},{"date":"from 1850s","references":[]}],"glosses":["Possessing beauty, impressing the eye; attractive.","Used emphatically or ironically, after the noun it qualifies."]},{"examples":[{"text":"He was a beautiful person; he would drop everything to help you.","bold_text_offsets":[[9,18]],"type":"example"},{"text":"You've done a beautiful thing today.","bold_text_offsets":[[14,23]],"type":"example"}],"glosses":["That one likes very much."]},{"examples":[{"text":"Beethoven's most beautiful sonata","bold_text_offsets":[[17,26]],"type":"example"},{"text":"It's beautiful outside, let's go for a walk.","bold_text_offsets":[[5,14]],"type":"example"},{"text":"These carnations smell beautiful but those daffodils smell funny.","bold_text_offsets":[[23,32]],"type":"example"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 1860s","references":[]}],"glosses":["Affording pleasure to any of the senses, especially that of hearing; delightful."]},{"examples":[{"text":"The skater performed a beautiful axel.","bold_text_offsets":[[23,32]],"type":"example"}],"attestations":[{"date":"from 1580s","references":[]}],"glosses":["Impressing with charm in an intellectual or moral way, through inherent suitability or elegance."]}],"pos":"adj","head_templates":[{"name":"en-adj","args":{},"expansion":"beautiful (comparative more beautiful, superlative most beautiful)"}],"forms":[{"form":"more beautiful","tags":["comparative"]},{"form":"most beautiful","tags":["superlative"]}],"translations":[{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"attractive","tags":["masculine"],"word":"beau"},{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"attractive","tags":["feminine"],"word":"belle"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"attractive","word":"schön"},{"lang":"Greek","code":"el","lang_code":"el","sense":"attractive","roman":"oraíos","word":"ωραίος"},{"lang":"Greek","code":"el","lang_code":"el","sense":"attractive","roman":"ómorfos","word":"όμορφος"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"attractive","word":"hermoso"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"attractive","word":"fermoso"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"attractive","word":"bello"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"attractive","word":"bel"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"attractive","word":"bellido"},{"lang":"French","code":"fr","lang_code":"fr","sense":"of weather: pleasant, clear","tags":["masculine"],"word":"beau"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"of weather: pleasant, clear","word":"heiter"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"of weather: pleasant, clear","word":"schön"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"of weather: pleasant, clear","word":"despejado"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"of weather: pleasant, clear","word":"alegre"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"as a pro-sentence","word":"toll"},{"lang":"Spanish","code":"es","lang_code":"es","sense":"as a pro-sentence","word":"bravo"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"used emphaticly or ironically","word":"toll"},{"lang":"German","code":"de","lang_code":"de","sense":"used emphaticly or ironically","word":"schön"}],"sounds":[{"tags":["UK"],"enpr":"byo͞oʹtĭ-fəl"},{"ipa":"/ˈbjuːtɪ.fəl/","tags":["UK"]},{"ipa":"/ˈbjuːtɪ.fʊl/","tags":["UK"]},{"audio":"En-uk-beautiful.ogg","tags":["UK"],"ogg_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/En-uk-beautiful.ogg","mp3_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ea/En-uk-beautiful.ogg/En-uk-beautiful.ogg.mp3"},{"tags":["US"],"ipa":"/ˈbju.tɪ.fəl/"},{"tags":["US"],"ipa":"[bju.ɾə.fəl]"},{"audio":"en-us-beautiful.ogg","tags":["US"],"ogg_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/En-us-beautiful.ogg","mp3_url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ea/En-us-beautiful.ogg/En-us-beautiful.ogg.mp3"}],"hyphenations":[{"parts":["beau","ti","ful"]}],"word":"beautiful","lang":"English","lang_code":"en"}
